    <string name="bt_pairing_note">While pairing, Windows shows the phone with a phone icon: that is normal (it uses the device class). When done, the phone must show up in Windows as connected; if it only says \"Paired\", remove it and pair again with MyMouse open on this Bluetooth screen.</string>
    <string name="bt_pairing_steps">To pair for the first time:\n1. Tap \"Make discoverable\" and keep this screen open.\n2. On Windows: Settings → Bluetooth &amp; devices → Add device → Bluetooth, and pick this phone.\n3. Confirm the code on both sides.\nAfter that, the phone connects to that PC by itself when you open MyMouse.\n\n%1$s</string>
    <string name="bt_pointer_note">The pointer is as smooth as the reports per second: this is the real interval between reports (not a ping: Bluetooth HID does not confirm what it sends). Settings → Bluetooth interval changes the pace (6–20 ms).</string>
    <string name="bt_repair_fine_scroll">If you change the smooth scroll setting or scrolling is jumpy, remove the phone in Windows and pair it again (Windows caches the mouse descriptor).</string>
    <string name="bt_repair_help">If you paired the phone before choosing Bluetooth in MyMouse: in Windows, Settings → Bluetooth → the phone → Remove device; here, Make discoverable; and add it again from Windows.</string>
